    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) headlining the lineup as the clear top play. His elite score is driven by a favorable matchup against Michael McGreevy, where his sprint speed potential and lead-off spot maximize his contribution to our most scarce category: stolen bases. Following him, **Yordan Alvarez** (66.84) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.79) anchor the core, providing high-floor production against their respective left-handed matchups. **Lars Nootbaar** (64.61) also warrants attention; despite a pedestrian base projection, he receives a significant boost from an favorable matchup against Grant Holmes, making him a high-efficiency start in our outfield mix.\n\nSeveral tactical edges are influencing today's configuration. **Dillon Dingler** (63.90) and **Junior Caminero** (64.47) benefit from positive platoon dynamics and prime order placement, which have pushed them into \"Strong\" start territory. Conversely, **Kazuma Okamoto** (40.13) sits right on the cusp of our threshold; his score is hampered significantly by a difficult matchup against Cam Schlittler (2.81 xERA), forcing us to keep him in the lineup only due to a lack of superior alternatives. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (45.27), who fell just shy of the cutoff. While his platoon advantage is favorable, the optimizer favored the higher overall volume and order stability provided by the likes of **Caleb Durbin** and **Chase Meidroth**.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given that all lineups are currently pending. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** carries a 37% rain risk that we must monitor closely as first pitch approaches, as a delay or cancellation would severely damage our stolen base potential for the day. Additionally, while **Trea Turner** (63.78) provides high-end utility, we must be cautious of his matchup against Connor Prielipp, whose delivery style creates a slight drag on **Trea Turner**'s efficiency in the base-stealing department. We are proceeding with the current construction, but owners should be prepared to pivot if official lineup releases deviate significantly from our projected batting orders.",
